From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: LR/CTR moves cost more than memory on the Cell PPE

GCC 16 under register pressure keeps loop values in the link register
(mtlr rX ... mflr rY) instead of saving one more callee-saved GPR or
spilling to the stack.  Moves to and from LR are slow on the Cell PPE.
On PS3 hardware a pixman 8888-with-a8-mask composite ran 6.9% slower
than the GCC 12.4 build; its hot combiner (combine_over_u) carries such
moves inside the loop.  Across the SDK and portlibs GCC 16 emitted 1039
LR-as-register moves against GCC 12.4's 205.

rs6000_register_move_cost already prices LR/CTR moves above memory for
POWER6-POWER9, so the allocator spills to memory there; add the Cell
tuning (PROCESSOR_CELL, the powerpc64-ps3-elf default) to that list.

diff --git a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
index 678d620..e1619bd 100644
--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
@@ -23037,7 +23037,10 @@ rs6000_register_move_cost (machine_mode mode,
       else if ((rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_POWER6
 		|| rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_POWER7
 		|| rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_POWER8
-		|| rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_POWER9)
+		|| rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_POWER9
+		/* The Cell PPE too: GCC 16 otherwise parks values in LR
+		   (mtlr/mflr pairs, inside loops) where GCC 12 spilled them.  */
+		|| rs6000_tune == PROCESSOR_CELL)
 	       && reg_class_subset_p (rclass, SPECIAL_REGS))
         ret = 6 * hard_regno_nregs (FIRST_GPR_REGNO, mode);
 
